d 'ADTEST': module to perform a k-sample Anderson-Darling equality-of-distributions test
d
d  adtest performs a (optionally weighted) k-sample
d Anderson-Darling (AD) permutation test to assess whether k >= 2
d samples come from the same distribution, as proposed by Scholz
d and Stephens (1987). It is the k-sample generalization of the
d two-sample Anderson and Darling test (1952).	When k > 2, there
d is no single pairwise comparison to make, so adtest instead
d compares each group's empirical CDF to the (weighted) pooled
d empirical CDF of all groups combined. 
d
d KW: equality of distributions
d KW: k-sample
d KW: comparisons
d KW: weighting
d
d Requires: Stata version 11
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260805
d
d Author: Ariel Linden, Linden Consulting Group, LLC
d Support: email alinden@@lindenconsulting.org
d
f adtest.ado
f adtest.sthlp
